/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Link: <https://www.cloudcertprep.io/license.xml>; rel="license"
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cloud.umami.is https://analytics.cloudcertprep.io https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://cloud.umami.is https://analytics.cloudcertprep.io https://gateway.umami.is https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# CSP NOTE: the `'unsafe-inline'` tokens in script-src AND style-src above are
# BUILD-TIME PLACEHOLDERS. The postbuild step `scripts/generate-csp-hashes.mjs`
# rewrites the dist/_headers copy of this CSP:
#   - script-src: 'unsafe-inline' -> exhaustive 'sha256-...' hashes of every
#     inline <script> in dist/**/*.html (security V2/V13).
#   - style-src: 'unsafe-inline' -> 'unsafe-hashes' + 'sha256-...' hashes of
#     every inline <style> ELEMENT and every style="" ATTRIBUTE value in the
#     built HTML. 'unsafe-hashes' lets the attr hashes match (Chrome 69+,
#     Firefox 109+, Safari 15.4+); older browsers degrade cosmetically only
#     (halo/progress-bar inline styles), never functionally. style-src-elem/
#     -attr split was rejected: Safari shipped style-src-elem only in 26.2,
#     so the split would regress most Safari users to the style-src fallback.
#   - connect-src: the https://*.supabase.co + wss://*.supabase.co wildcards
#     are pinned to the exact project host derived from VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#     (shrinks the exfil surface if XSS ever slips the hash CSP).
# The host-source allowlists (umami / cloudflare / cloudflareinsights) stay so
# the dynamically-injected Umami, Turnstile, and Cloudflare Web Analytics
# scripts keep loading. CF Web Analytics loads beacon.min.js from
# static.cloudflareinsights.com and posts to cloudflareinsights.com (the zone
# auto-injects it now that DNS is on Cloudflare). analytics.cloudcertprep.io is
# the self-hosted Umami instance (serves script.js, receives same-origin
# /api/send posts); it is used when VITE_UMAMI_HOST points the BaseLayout beacon
# there instead of Umami Cloud. GA stays disabled, so
# googletagmanager / google-analytics are intentionally NOT allowlisted; re-add
# them (script-src + connect-src) if GA is ever re-enabled.
# Edit inline scripts/styles freely; hashes regenerate on every build.

# Static assets have content-hashed filenames (e.g. index.A8f2k3.js), so they
# are safe to cache forever. New deploys produce new hashes => new filenames.
# Astro emits ALL hashed assets under /_astro/ (there is no dist/assets/) —
# a previous /assets/* rule here matched nothing and every hashed chunk missed
# the immutable cache.
# NOTE: no `/*` Cache-Control rule is set. Cloudflare Pages MERGES every
# matching `_headers` rule rather than letting a more specific path override, so
# a `/*` `max-age=0` would combine with this immutable rule and defeat long-term
# caching of hashed assets. HTML routes fall back to the default (revalidated)
# caching, which is correct for one-HTML-file-per-route output.
# (This `_headers` file applies to the /_astro/* responses that _routes.json
# excludes from the Pages Function; HTML routes get their headers from the
# Function in functions/_middleware.js instead.)
# (public/fonts/og/ is satori build input only — never client-served, no rule.)
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
